<title>BULGARIA: Yield falls on Bulgaria 3-mth discount T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Bulgaria 3-mth discount T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield to maturity on Bulgaria's Finance ministry three-month discount T-bills fell to 8.32 percent at Monday's auction from 9.81 percent a week earlier, central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Today's issue was offered with a par value of nine billion levs and no minimum acceptable price set in advance.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		 BG3034397003</p>
<p> Maturity		     three months</p>
<p> Par value		    9.0 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date		 May 19</p>
<p> Issue date		   May 21</p>
<p> Maturity date		August 20</p>
<p> Bids received		8,623 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	  91.89 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		7,200 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	 92.32 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity    8.32 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
</text>
